re sits at 0.5, so one year like that counts as half a year of full health."}, {"draw": ["p_new", "n_new", "l_new", "hop", "l_hop"], "speak": "On the new treatment, q rises to 0.7."}, {"pause": 0.4}, {"point": {"at": {"ref": "p_dead"}, "gesture": "underline"}, "speak": "The scale does not stop at zero."}, {"draw": ["band_worse", "l_worse"], "speak": "When people are asked, many rate the worst states, such as extreme pain with no ability to move or wash, as worse than being dead, so those get a weight below 0."}, {"draw": ["p_worst", "n_worst", "l_worst"], "speak": "In the first UK value set for the EQ-5D questionnaire, the worst state scored about minus 0.59."}, {"highlight": {"target": ["n_std", "n_new"]}, "speak": "Where numbers like 0.5 and 0.7 come from is the next lecture's question; here, take them as given."}, {"highlight": {"target": ["p_std", "n_std"], "effect": "circle"}, "speak": "So q is an exchange rate: it says how many years of full health one year in that state is worth."}]}, "template_gaps": [{"template": "number_line", "missing": "point labels and tick numerals are not drawn with their point's beat (they appear only at the end), text is small and close points' labels collide; no vertical orientation"}]}